From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: shell32: Keep New in filesystem background menus

The Inventor Open shell view queries command IDs 0 through 0x7fff. Windows 10 build 19045.6466 showed an enabled New submenu in that range on both architectures. Wine rebases the resource IDs by -0x7000, so the old popup ID 0x42 wraps out of range before its children can be merged.

Move only the New popup into the background command ID range. Require a creation helper and a filesystem-backed parent. Do not use a missing PIDL when creation fails. Leave the other popups and the shared menu merge function alone.

v2 (2026-11-18): Cross review found that Recycle Bin implements ISFHelper with stub creation methods. Require a filesystem path and exercise that Wine-specific virtual-folder case. Skip the measured English caption check in other UI languages.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.
